{
  "email": "dana.whitfield@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket from Dana Whitfield: Outlook desktop not receiving new mail since this morning while phone works. Checking account, devices, and mailbox usage per KB-009."
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-LT-0101",
  "reason": "Checking whether Dana Whitfield's laptop is online and healthy per KB-009 quick check, since Outlook desktop is not receiving mail."
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, I checked your account and it looks healthy: your mailbox has plenty of room and your laptop is online with no warnings, so the problem is most likely in the Outlook app on the laptop. Please try these steps in order. First, open Outlook on the web in a browser and tell us whether new mail is showing there. If it is, go back to the laptop and check that Work Offline is turned off (Send / Receive tab), then close Outlook completely and reopen it. If mail still doesn't arrive, restart the laptop. If it is still stuck after that, let us know and we can walk you through rebuilding your Outlook profile. Please reply with what you see on the web version, since that tells us whether the issue is with the mailbox or the laptop.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user for dana.whitfield (user_id 1, CEO, VIP, active, not blocked, 0 failed logins, mailbox 17.4% of 50 GB). check_device_status on BL-LT-0101: online, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:57 UTC, 60.5% disk free, no warnings. Mailbox full and laptop offline ruled out. Not yet confirmed: whether Outlook on the web shows the new mail (KB-009 step 1), and whether other users are affected (no outage reported). Asked user to run the KB-009 quick checks and fix steps (web check, Work Offline, restart, profile rebuild). Escalate to Tier 2 if OWA also shows no new mail or if other users report the same issue. Not checked: sign-in logs and Duo, since the account shows no lockout or block and the phone syncs fine.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-009",
    "KB-010"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
